🎯 Suggested Fix: Hybrid Multimodal Search
To resolve the Ghost Vector issue, I suggest updating the search_document method in runner.py to use Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF). This allows the system to actually utilize the image embeddings:

Python
from qdrant_client import models

def search_document(self, question: str):
    query_vector = self.embedder.embed_text(question)
    
    # Perform Hybrid Search (Text + Image Vectors)
    results = self.qdrant_client.query_points(
        collection_name=self.collection_name,
        prefetch=[
            models.Prefetch(query=query_vector, using="text", limit=self.top_k),
            models.Prefetch(query=query_vector, using="image", limit=self.top_k)
        ],
        query=models.FusionQuery(fusion=models.Fusion.RRF),
        score_threshold=self.score_threshold,
        with_payload=True
    ).points
    
    return results
✅ Positive Observations
Resilient Fallbacks: The try-except block in runner.py for "named vectors" is an excellent defense against schema mismatches.

Clean Orchestration: The use of factory patterns makes the system highly testable and easy to extend.

Precise Chunking: Respecting sentence boundaries (rfind('. ')) ensures the LLM receives semantically complete context.

